Falsifies `timetable::proofs::an_nth_weekday_is_counted_from_its_month`.

The defect: the week of the month is counted from day 0, so the 7th, 14th, 21st and 28th are placed in the following week.

Expected to fail: the `assert_eq!` against counting, at `dom == 7` for `n == 1`.

diff --git a/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs b/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs
index e0cdeb116..9386eaa22 100644
--- a/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs
+++ b/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ pub fn month_day_matches(on: MonthDay, dom: u8, dow: u8, month_len: u8) -> bool
         MonthDay::Nth(n, want) => {
             dow == want
                 && if n > 0 {
-                    (dom - 1) / 7 + 1 == n as u8
+                    dom / 7 + 1 == n as u8
                 } else {
                     dom + 7 > month_len
                 }
